[thin] Required fixed insert seats within the selected smooth casing. Ordinary walls are Derek's specified 2.38 mm and the floor is 2 mm, both below this ranking's 2.5 mm sampling threshold. At the corner pilot the retained R11.7 outside round, fixed cap-clamp axis and Ø4 mm ruthex pilot leave 1.696 mm of radial stock. The manufacturer's RX-M3x5.7 geometry calls for 1.6 mm from the pilot to the outside. Exact full-depth annular witnesses pass for all twenty pilots and retain the same material as the mating reference shell. See foam-shell/prints/2026-10-26-mark2-round-ports-a2/insert-witnesses.json.
alternatives: Adding stock on the cavity side does not increase the pilot's minimum ligament to the outside round. Moving the pilot inward moves the common cap/lid screw pattern. Growing the exterior or changing its corner round changes the retained casing and enclosure fits. Reducing the Ø4 mm bore changes ruthex's specified pilot.
